    {
      "id": "7f7da011c084e129",
      "category": "technology",
      "title": "Accelerating MONAI Digital-Pathology Pipelines on AMD Instinct™ GPUs with hipCIM",
      "summary": "A digital-pathology model is only as fast as the pipeline that feeds it. That’s simple to overlook when the conversation turns to network architectures and FLOPs, but on real whole-slide workloads the truth is stubborn: a great deal of the wall-clock time goes to reading gigapixel slides off disk and decoding them into the small tiles the model consumes. Speed up the model and leave the reader untouched, and the pipeline barely moves.",
      "url": "https://rocm.blogs.amd.com/artificial-intelligence/monai-hipcim-2608/README.html",
      "source": "AMD ROCm Blog",
      "sourceCountry": "United States",
      "sourceType": "engineering",
